    {
      "text": "Zenos … spake concerning the three days of darkness, 1 Ne. 19:10 (Hel. 14:20, 27; 3 Ne. 8:3, 23). after he is laid in a sepulchre for … three days, 2 Ne. 25:13. eyes of none shall behold it save it be that three witnesses, 2 Ne. 27:12 (Ether 5:3; D&C 5:11). three days and three nights that I could not open my mouth, Alma 36:10. they did last for about … three hours, 3 Ne. 8:19. I spake concerning … three who were caught up into the heavens, 3 Ne. 28:36. disciples … had all gone to the paradise of God, save it were the three, 4 Ne. 1:14. Shared fought against him for … three days, Ether 13:28. three witnesses of the church did condemn them, Moro. 6:7.",
